          %title
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Rational function over an associative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            should be a class of expressions involving operations in noncommutative polynomial ring combined with the operation of formal inverse modulo which are evaluable for at least at some choice of variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            in a chosen associative algebra modulo identities which are true after evaluation at common evaluation points.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            The division ring of
            %strong noncommutative rational functions
            on a given alphabet is defined in Cohn’s book essentially as follows.
          %h3#noncommutative_rational_expressions Noncommutative rational expressions
          %p
            Given a commutative field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            (“field of constants”), and a finite set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \{x_1,\ldots,x_n\}
            (“alphabet”), consider the free algebra on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (in the sense of universal algebra) of signature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ +_2, \cdot_2, (\,)^{-1}_1, -_1\}
            and with constants in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and denote it by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}(X,k)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0^{-1}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-x)^{-1}
            are in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}(X,k)
            as no relations are imposed (one starts with terms which are elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\cup k
            and continues by nesting sequence of algebraic operations eventually connecting all terms). The elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}(X,k)
            are sometimes called noncommutative rational expressions on alphabet
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be an associative
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X\to R
            a map of sets. Then there is a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}_\phi \subset \mathcal{R}(X,k)
            (of
            = succeed "-\u201Cevaluables\u201D)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_* : \mathcal{R}_\phi\to R
            uniquely determined by the rules
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                (constants evaluate) If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in k
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℛ
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{R}_\phi
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(c) = c
            %li
              %p
                (variables evaluate) If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℛ
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{R}_\phi
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(x) = \phi(x)
            %li
              %p
                (sums, products and negatives of evaluables evaluate) If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℛ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g \in\mathcal{R}_\phi
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℛ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f+g, f\cdot g, -f \in\mathcal{R}_\phi
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(f+g) = \phi_*(f) + \phi_*(g)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi_*(f\cdot g) =
                      \\phi_*(f)\cdot\phi_*(g)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(-f) = -\phi_*(f)
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℛ
                          %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in \mathcal{R}_\phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(g)
                is invertible in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℛ
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{-1}\in \mathcal{R}_\phi
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(g^{-1}) = \phi_*(g)^{-1}
          %h3#domains Domains
          %p
            For every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in \mathcal{R}(X,k)
            define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Dom
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Dom}\,f
            to be the set of all
            = succeed "-tuples" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |X|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec{r} = (r_1,\ldots,r_{|X|}) \in R^{|X|}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in \mathcal{R}_\phi
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = \phi_{\vec{r}}
            satisfies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x_i) = r_i
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1,\ldots, |X|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Dom
                  %mi f
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Dom} f \neq \emptyset
            are called nondegenerate. It is clear that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∉
                  %msub
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \notin\mathcal{R}_\phi
            iff there is a subexpression in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_0)^{-1}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0 \in \mathcal{R}_\phi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_*(f_0)
            is not invertible in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %h3#equivalence_of_expressions Equivalence of expressions
          %p
            Two rational expressions with nonempty domains are equivalent if their domains have nonempty intersection and their evaluations agree at the intersection of domains, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\sim g
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Dom
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi Dom
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\vec{r}\in Dom\,f\cap Dom\,g
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{\vec{r}*}(f) = \phi_{\vec{r}*}(g)
          %h3#noncommutative_rational_functions Noncommutative rational functions
          %p
            The equivalence classes of noncommutative rational expressions with nonempty domain are called noncommutative rational functions in variables in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is an infinite field and under some conditions on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            over algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            naturally form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+ring"} division ring
            (skewfield).
          %h3#free_skewfield Free skewfield
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the matrix ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n(k)
            then all noncommutative rational functions in alphabet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            form a skewfield traditionally denoted by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\lt\!\!\!\!\!(\,X\!\!\gt\!\!\!\!\!)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[X]
          %p
            Amitsur considered instead
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = D
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is any skewfield which is infinite-dimensional over its center
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(D)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(D)
            is infinite as well. He obtained the universal field of fractions which does not depend on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in this construction either.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Cohn proved that if in the free skewfield any full matrix is invertible. An
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\times n
            matrix
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is full if it can not be factorized as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 A_2
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\times r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\times n
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt n
          %h2#literature Literature
          %p
            %strong Noncommutative rational identities
            are formally studied in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shimshon+Amitsur"}> S. A. Amitsur
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rational identities and application to algebra and geometry
              %strong 3
              (1966) 304–359.
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.+M.+Cohn"}> P. M. Cohn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Free rings and their relations
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+M.+Bergman"}> George M. Bergman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rational relations and rational identities in division rings. I
              %strong 43
              (1976) 252–266
          %p The division ring of noncommutative rational functions on a given alphabet is defined in Cohn’s book.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+M.+Bergman"}> George M. Bergman
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Skew fields of noncommutative rational functions, after Amitsur
